## Prepare without generating

Read `GET /v1/quest/catalog` for your assignment’s capabilities, limits, write policy and price. Create a session with `POST /v1/quest/sessions` and a saved `Idempotency-Key`. Task kinds are `homework`, `practice`, `exam_prep` and `open`.

```json
{
  "setup": {
    "task": {
      "kind": "practice",
      "subject": "Fractions",
      "assignment": "Compare fractions using equivalent denominators."
    },
    "learner": {
      "preferred_name": "Sample learner",
      "grade_band": "middle",
      "language": "en"
    },
    "display_name": "Maple",
    "team_dialog": false
  }
}
```

Save the returned `session_id`. The task, the learner preferences and the tutor’s name are fixed for this session. Preparing a session uses no free attempt and no charge. Use a new session for a different task. Responses use US English.

An ordinary first message is learner input. Request a generated opening explicitly with `quest.operation: "opening"` and an empty prompt. A generated opening is a turn; do not replace a learner’s actual first message with it.

## Keep the receipt

Every turn has a request id and ends with two records you can keep.

- `done.commercial` is the charge: `billable_units` is 0 or 1; `charge.amount_micro_usd` is the amount charged, in millionths of a dollar, and is zero whenever `billable_units` is 0; `settlement` is `reserved`, `settled` or `released`, and a released charge is always zero; `request_id`, `listing`, `band` and `rate_version` say which request and which rate.
- `quest_receipt.receipt` is the turn: `posture` is the kind of help that served it (`guided`, `feedback`, `explain` or `diagnostic`); `turn_index` is its place in the session; `team_dialog` says whether frame text may be shown; `composition_hash` and `mode` identify exactly what served it; `repairs` and `validation_failures` are short form codes and are empty on an ordinary turn.

A cost meter needs only the `done` events:

```
// Call this with the final "done" event of every request your server completes.
const seen = new Set();
let turns = 0, microUsd = 0;
function record(done) {
  const { request_id, billable_units, charge } = done.commercial;
  if (seen.has(request_id)) return;   // a replay of the same request is not a second charge
  seen.add(request_id);
  turns += billable_units;
  microUsd += charge.amount_micro_usd; // zero for a turn that failed or was free
}
const dollars = () => microUsd / 1_000_000;
```

